ople have no fingerprints, and why some people survive nuclear bombs. Genes illuminate everything from JFK's bronze skin (it wasn't a tan) to Einstein's genius. They prove that Neanderthals and humans bred thousands of years more recently than any of us would feel comfortable thinking. They can even allow some people, because of the exceptional flexibility of their thumbs and fingers, to become truly singular violinists. Kean's vibrant storytelling once again makes science entertaining, explaining human history and whimsy while showing how DNA will influence our species' future\"--"},"covers":[8260170],"local_id":["urn:sfpl:31223100112375","urn:sfpl:31223094938231","urn:sfpl:31223094937050","urn:sfpl:31223100112219","urn:sfpl:31223094937043","urn:sfpl:31223094937068","urn:sfpl:31223100112235","urn:sfpl:31223100112102","urn:sfpl:31223094938017","urn:sfpl:31223094938223","urn:sfpl:31223094938140","urn:sfpl:31223094938082","urn:sfpl:31223094938124","urn:sfpl:31223100112367","urn:sfpl:31223094938108","urn:sfpl:31223100949602","urn:sfpl:31223100949677","urn:sfpl:31223100949636","urn:sfpl:31223100112334"],"lc_classifications":["QH437 .K43 2012","QH437.K43 2012","QH431 .K24 2012"],"key":"/books/OL25282616M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL6758454A"}],"ocaid":"violiniststhumbo00kean","publish_places":["New York"],"isbn_13":["9780316182317"],"pagination":"p. cm.","source_records":["marc:marc_loc_updates/v40.i16.records.utf8:11942022:1755","marc:marc_loc_updates/v40.i20.records.utf8:13267852:1800","marc:marc_loc_updates/v40.i22.records.utf8:12902044:1766","ia:violiniststhumbo00kean","marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run04.mrc:248252878:7448","bwb:9780316182317","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part39.utf8:179438512:1802","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.13.20150123.full.mrc:390852960:3591","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_020.bib.mrc:263395208:4488"],"title":"The violinist's thumb","lccn":["2012007029"],"notes":{"typ